      "hints": [
        "Gradient formula: $\\frac{b - 1}{a + 1} = 2 \\implies b = 2a + 3$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the gradient formula between $A(-1, 1)$ and $P(a, b)$:\n$$m_{AP} = \\frac{b - 1}{a - (-1)} = \\frac{b - 1}{a + 1} = 2$$",
        "Rearrange to express $b$ explicitly in terms of $a$:\n$$b - 1 = 2(a + 1) = 2a + 2 \\implies b = 2a + 3$$"
      ],
