      "hints": [
        "Find $AB^2 = 11^2 + (-2)^2 = 125$.",
        "Set $(a + 1)^2 + (b - 1)^2 = 125$, substitute $b - 1 = 2(a + 1) \\implies 5(a + 1)^2 = 125$.",
        "Solve to find $P(4, 11)$ and $P(-6, -9)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the square of the distance between $A(-1, 1)$ and $B(10, -1)$:\n$$AB^2 = (10 - (-1))^2 + (-1 - 1)^2 = 11^2 + (-2)^2 = 121 + 4 = 125$$",
        "Set $AP^2 = AB^2 = 125$ using the distance formula for $P(a, b)$:\n$$(a + 1)^2 + (b - 1)^2 = 125$$",
        "Substitute $b - 1 = 2(a + 1)$ into the distance equation:\n$$(a + 1)^2 + [2(a + 1)]^2 = 125 \\implies (a + 1)^2 + 4(a + 1)^2 = 125$$\n$$5(a + 1)^2 = 125 \\implies (a + 1)^2 = 25$$\n$$a + 1 = 5 \\implies a = 4 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a + 1 = -5 \\implies a = -6$$",
        "Calculate the corresponding values of $b = 2a + 3$:\n$$\\text{For } a = 4: \\quad b = 2(4) + 3 = 11 \\implies (4, 11)$$\n$$\\text{For } a = -6: \\quad b = 2(-6) + 3 = -9 \\implies (-6, -9)$$\n$$\\text{Possible coordinates of } P: \\quad (4, 11) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad (-6, -9)$$"
      ],
